   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I don&#39;t have anything to add but I too would like to know how to speed up doing a zero inflated model in stan. I have similar code to Guido&#39;s, but with the addition of fixed effects for year and country, but the sampling is one of the slowest I have experienced for a stan model. Help is wanted!</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, October 15, 2015 at 11:09:30 AM UTC-4, Guido Biele wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I am working with a zero-inflated negative binomial model in which I so far </div><div>loop through cases as shown in the stan language reference.</div><div>here is a snippet from the model block.</div><div>(I am leaving out the other parts of the model, which essentially follow</div><div>the example model for a hierarchical model with multivariate priors </div><div>from the stan documentation )</div><div><div> </div></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    theta_n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dot_product</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sx0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    eta_n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> dot_product</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    phi_n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">==</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log_sum_exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                             </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> neg_binomial_2_log_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">else</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> neg_binomial_2_log_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>There are some things I could do to vectorize, but I am </div><div>uncertain if this would lead to a noticeable speed improvement.</div><div>Maybe somebody with the relevant knowledge can comment on this?</div><div><br></div><div>Please note that I did not test this code, so there are nearly certainly bugs in it.</div><div><br></div><div>A)</div><div>split cases according to zero and nonzero outcomes (y)</div><div>and calculate theta and eta outside the without looping through participants,</div><div>something like:<br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">real theta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N</span><span style=\"color:#660\">];</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">row_vector</span></font><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span></font><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> eta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">row_vector</span></font><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span></font><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">row_vector</span></font><font color=\"#666600\"><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span></font><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phis</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sx0 </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the design matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha are the regression weights<br></span><font color=\"#008800\"><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> I am </span><span style=\"color:#008\">using</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the same regression weights </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> all groups </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> the zero inflation part of the model</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">theta </span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sx0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> loop throug M groups </span><span style=\"color:#008\">with</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> different regression weights </span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group_start contains indices indicating </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> which row a </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> starts<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> group_size contains integers indicating </span><span style=\"color:#008\">group</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sizes<br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  eta </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">beta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">block</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sx</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_start</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">\\\\</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> now split eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">and</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theta according to whether the criterion y </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> zero<br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> eta_zero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">segment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_start_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> theta_zero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">segment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_start_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> eta_nonzero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">segment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_start_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> theta_nonzero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">segment</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_start_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> phi_nonzero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_nonzero</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep_row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br> phi_zero </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> append_row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_zero</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep_row_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">group_size_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">k</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><div><br></div>I could not figure out quickly how to initialize an empty vector, </div><div>and I don&#39;t think that one broadcast into segments of a vector.</div><div>Therefore I use the ugly trick to start with a small vector that I then expand it ...<br><div><br></div></div><div>B) </div><div>Loop through zero y (because of the need to use log_sum_exp),</div><div>but use vectorization for nonzero y (I know this doesn&#39;t improve</div><div>the speed of increment_log_prob, but hope it makes </div><div>neg_binomial_2_log_log faster ...).</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">log_sum_exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                                                    bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                                                    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> neg_binomial_2_log_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">],</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_zero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>increment_log_prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">bernoulli_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tail</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">theta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> neg_binomial_2_log_log</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tail</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">eta_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tail</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phi_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">N_nonzero</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)));</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>What do you think?</div><div><br></div><div>Guido</div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
